// REJECTS: Expected jsonSchema bsonType should be of object type
//
// A `jsonSchema:` whose top-level `bsonType` is "string" rather than "object". The JSON is
// well-formed, double-quoted correctly, and lexes and parses without complaint -- and
// MongoDBSchemaParseTreeWalker.getSchemaExpression then runs MongoDBSchemaDeserializer over
// it AT PARSE TIME and refuses a non-object root.
//
// So a string literal's semantic content, interpreted by a Jackson deserializer, decides
// whether a .pure file parses. Nothing about that is expressible in a .g4, and a rewrite that
// stores the schema text verbatim and defers deserialization to compile time -- the obviously
// correct layering -- is more permissive here.
//
// Unrecognised keys inside the schema are silently IGNORED by the same deserializer, so the
// permissiveness is genuinely selective and cannot be reproduced by validating the JSON
// against a strict schema either. See ../fixtures/t2-mongodb.pure, which carries a deliberate
// ignored key.
###MongoDB
Database fixture::neg::NonObjectSchema
(
  Collection Person
  (
    jsonSchema: {
      "bsonType": "string"
    };
  )
)
